---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import BackToTop from '../components/BackToTop.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service - SecureVault">
  <div class="premium-container" id="main-container">
    <SiteHeader />

    <main>
      <section class="page-header">
        <h1 class="headline">Terms of service</h1>
        <p class="subheadline">The deal, in plain words.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="legal-content">
        <div class="text-block">
          <p>
            SecureVault is a free app for Android that keeps photos, videos and
            notes in an encrypted vault behind an everyday app. It shows no ads
            and sells nothing. These terms are the agreement between you and us
            when you use it.
          </p>
          <p>
            Last updated on 18 November 2026. How the app handles your data is
            in its <a href={`${base}/privacy/`}>privacy policy</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            SecureVault is published by Chaosmos, the studio Shravan Goswami
            runs. "We" and "us" in these terms mean Chaosmos (Shravan Goswami).
            Jash Ambaliya and Jitendra Verma created the original app with him.
            You can reach us at
            <a href="mailto:hello@chaosmos.studio">hello@chaosmos.studio</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Agreeing to these terms</h2>
          <p>
            By installing or using SecureVault, you agree to these terms. If you
            do not agree, please do not use it. If you are under the age at which
            you can agree to terms like these where you live, a parent or
            guardian needs to agree for you.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Using the app</h2>
          <p>
            We give you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to
            install SecureVault and use it on your own devices. The app, its
            design and its code belong to us. Please do not copy, sell or
            redistribute it, and do not reverse engineer it except as the law
            allows.
          </p>
          <p>
            Use SecureVault lawfully. Do not use it to keep anything that is
            illegal to have, or to hide anything that harms other people.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Your vault and your PIN</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Everything you put in a vault stays on your phone, encrypted with
              your PIN. We never receive it and cannot see it.
            </li>
            <li>
              We cannot recover a forgotten PIN or anything locked behind it.
              Choose a PIN you will remember.
            </li>
            <li>
              Uninstalling the app, resetting the phone or clearing the app's
              storage deletes your vaults. Back up your vault from the app's
              settings and keep the file somewhere safe.
            </li>
            <li>
              The disguise changes how the app looks on your phone. It does not
              stop someone who knows your PIN, or who has full control of your
              phone, from reaching your vault.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Changes to the app</h2>
          <p>
            We keep improving SecureVault. Updates can add, change or remove
            features, and we may one day stop offering the app.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>The app as it is</h2>
          <p>
            We make SecureVault with care, but we provide it as it is, without
            promises that it will always be available or free of bugs, as far as
            the law allows. As far as the law allows, we are not liable for lost
            data, for indirect or unforeseeable losses, or for losses that come
            from a forgotten PIN or a missing backup.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Your rights under the law</h2>
          <p>
            Nothing in these terms takes away rights you have under the consumer
            protection laws where you live, including in the European Economic
            Area and the United Kingdom. Where these terms and those laws differ,
            the laws win.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>The law that applies</h2>
          <p>
            These terms are governed by the laws of India. If you live
            elsewhere, you keep the protection of the laws of your own country,
            and you can bring a claim in your own courts where those laws allow.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
          <p>
            If these terms change, this page will be updated and the date at the
            top will change.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Email <a href="mailto:hello@chaosmos.studio">hello@chaosmos.studio</a>
            with any question about these terms.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>

    <BackToTop />
    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  main {
    padding: 6rem 5% 4rem;
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    z-index: 2;
    position: relative;
  }
  .page-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }
  .headline {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .subheadline {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .legal-content {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 20px;
    padding: 2.5rem;
  }
  .text-block {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  p,
  li {
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .legal-content {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
